The included setup works for building RPM packages on Redhat RHEL 9.

Initial tasks:

Enable use repositories for Codeready Builder and EPEL.

Then install prerequisites:

$ sudo dnf install -y git rpmdevtools gcc gcc-c++ bison flex make coreutils systemd-devel
$ sudo dnf install -y libtool autoconf automake asciidoc xmlto autoconf-archive
$ sudo dnf install -y openssl-devel zlib-devel openldap-devel libcurl-devel
$ sudo dnf install -y gmime30-devel mhash-devel libevent-devel jemalloc-devel
$ sudo dnf install -y libsqlite3x-devel mariadb-devel postgresql-devel
$ sudo yum install -y clang15
$ sudo update-alternatives --install /usr/bin/cc cc /usr/bin/clang-15 50

Next, set up the build environment:

$ rpmdev-setuptree

Copy the spec files from this directory to ~/rpmbuild/SPECS/

Then fetch the source kits:

$ spectool -g ~/rpmbuild/SPECS/libsieve.spec -C ~/rpmbuild/SOURCES/
$ spectool -g ~/rpmbuild/SPECS/libzdb.spec -C ~/rpmbuild/SOURCES/
$ spectool -g ~/rpmbuild/SPECS/dbmail.spec -C ~/rpmbuild/SOURCES/

Finally, it's build time:

$ rpmbuild -ba rpmbuild/SPECS/libsieve.spec
$ sudo rpm -i rpmbuild/RPMS/x86_64/libsieve-2.2-2.el9.x86_64.rpm
$ sudo rpm -i rpmbuild/RPMS/x86_64/libsieve-devel-2.2-2.el9.x86_64.rpm
$ rpmbuild -ba rpmbuild/SPECS/libzdb.spec
$ sudo rpm -i rpmbuild/RPMS/x86_64/libzdb-3.2.3-2.el9.x86_64.rpm
$ sudo rpm -i rpmbuild/RPMS/x86_64/libzdb-devel-3.2.3-2.el9.x86_64.rpm
$ rpmbuild -ba rpmbuild/SPECS/dbmail.spec
$ sudo rpm -i rpmbuild/RPMS/x86_64/dbmail-3.5.4-2.el9.x86_64.rpm
$ sudo rpm -i rpmbuild/RPMS/x86_64/dbmail-auth-ldap-3.5.4-2.el9.x86_64.rpm

You now have DBmail installed and ready to go.
